      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path:</strong> Active bilateral exchange confirmed (<span class="cite">F3</span> YES); Hormuz formally closed at near-zero transits (<span class="cite">F4</span> 5%); diplomacy suspended with five days to <span class="cite">F1</span> horizon; IRGC autonomous messaging without MFA moderation. Military tempo shows no deceleration within current indicators.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path:</strong> Neither side has achieved decisive military objectives; US and Iranian strike exchanges remain within a calibrated threshold (bases, not capitals); backchannel Qatar/Pakistan contacts continue, preserving a latent de-escalation architecture. MCM operations partially established (<span class="cite">F5</span> PARTIAL) and could resume under a freeze.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path:</strong> Requires a ceasefire offer accepted by both sides, IRGC closure lifted (<span class="cite">F8</span> 22% within 14 days), and Iran rescinding June 1 suspension (<span class="cite">F1</span> 10%). All three conditions in conjunction sit well below 10%; 10% reflects tail probability of a surprise backchannel breakthrough not captured in current indicators.</p>
    </div>
